WEBVTT

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.350
Returning to normal space.

00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:16.320
Approaching El Facil.

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:18.950
Good. Begin preparations to dock.

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:20.050
Understood.

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:22.480
You two, prepare to unload the cargo.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:23.000
Yes, sir.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:23.570
Roger.

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:27.320
Hey, was Rudolf really that evil?

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:30.870
Are you reading history books again?

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:34.850
Why would everyone obey such a bad guy?

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:39.940
Well, the thing is, Rudolf 
was so good at being bad

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:41.850
that he fooled everyone.

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:45.300
But why were they all fooled?

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.180
You don't look satisfied with that answer.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:58.660
It's because the people wanted 
their lives to be easy.

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:04.750
<i>Yang Wen-li, who made a name 
for himself as a tactician</i>

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:08.090
<i>and became known as the 
"Unbeatable Magician,"</i>

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:13.280
<i>lived most of his life prior 
to age 16 on a spaceship</i>

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.980
<i>with his father, who was a trader.</i>

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:47.020
<b>Legend of the Galactic Heroes</b>

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:00.310
A soldier who likes to read?

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:01.890
No way.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:39.350
What is a cadet doing here?

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:44.290
Are cadets not allowed at the city library?

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:46.750
Of course they are,

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:49.740
but I've never seen any 
come here in uniform.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:52.180
Oh...

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:54.080
This is embarrassing.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.370
It's nothing to be embarrassed about.

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:00.040
You're pretty strange.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:03.050
How embarrassing...

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:06.270
You really are weird.

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:10.960
Wait, aren't you... "Empty-handed Yang"?

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:13.720
How do you know that nickname?

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:15.800
I knew it! I was right!

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:19.480
You moved into your dorm with no 
luggage, hence "Empty-handed Yang"!

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:23.370
But how do you know who I am?

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:28.060
The answer to that will be along soon.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:29.490
Let's wait for it together.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:36.670
There are many books here that 
we don't have at the school.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:37.780
Such as?

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:39.810
Such as...

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:42.170
books on the history of tea,

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:45.020
and books on the origin of that 
instrument you were playing.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:49.470
With a bit of searching, you can even 
find the diary of Rudolf's cook.

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:53.140
For an "empty-handed" guy, 
you're certainly diligent in your studies.

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:56.740
You just barely have passing grades in 
everything except military history,

00:04:57.140 --> 00:05:00.260
but the oddball Yang doesn't 
let that get to him.

00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:03.670
You really do know everything about me.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:06.400
This wasn't what I intended, though.

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:10.090
I'd planned to get into the 
university's history department,

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:11.930
but then my father died...

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:14.510
So the only way to learn about 
history without financial aid

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:17.770
was the Fleet Academy's graduate 
course on military history.

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:22.040
You really are unusual.

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:24.730
I'm not "really" anything.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:26.490
But that aside—

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:27.260
Yang?

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:29.590
Jean?

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:32.720
I wouldn't have expected 
to see you two together.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:36.550
You're late. We just met.

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:41.130
This is Jessica Edwards.

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:44.180
She's the Fleet Academy bursar's daughter,

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:46.150
and she attends a music school.

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:48.330
I've known her since we were kids.

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:50.780
That explains it.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:52.300
Why the death glare?

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.180
Something terrible happened!

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:56.880
What the heck does that mean?

00:05:57.370 --> 00:06:01.380
<b>Episode 4</b>

00:05:57.370 --> 00:06:01.380
<b>The Unbeatable Magician</b>

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:05.540
You certainly are different, Yang. 
You're such a history buff.

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:08.960
Come on, Jessica. 
Don't tease Yang like that.

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:13.860
But I finally got to meet the 
"Empty-handed Yang" you told me about!

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:17.570
Hey, tell me something interesting.

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:21.070
Well, I can't guarantee 
it'll be interesting...

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:27.560
When I was a boy, every book I read said the 
emperor Rudolf was a heinous villain.

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:30.850
I wondered how he became the emperor,

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:33.050
so I asked my father.

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:35.240
What did he say?

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:38.880
That it was because the people 
wanted their lives to be easy.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:40.950
They wanted their lives to be easy?

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:45.470
Rather than solving their 
problems on their own,

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:51.370
they were waiting for some 
superhero or saint to show up

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:52.940
and take it all on single-handedly.

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:55.850
Rudolf took advantage of that.

00:06:56.710 --> 00:06:58.960
Now, remember this.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:03.350
It is the people who create the dictator
who have the greater responsibility.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.290
Even if they don't actively support him,

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:09.060
standing by silently makes 
them equally guilty.

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:17.370
Free Planets Fleet Academy

00:07:22.430 --> 00:07:26.500
The head of the class will be 
in the next combat simulation.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:28.420
It's Wideborn's turn, huh?

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:29.290
Yeah.

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:32.620
What poor sap got matched up with him?

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:38.670
<i>The mock battle for combat simulation 
number 39 will now begin.</i>

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:49.940
Malcolm Wideborn

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:49.940
Reorganize the fleet into 
a spindle formation.

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:52.840
Reorganizing fleet into 
a spindle formation.

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:54.420
All ships, advance!

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:56.010
All ships, advance!

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.620
Wideborn's fleet is advancing.

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:02.930
Execute Plan C.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.350
Executing Plan C.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:09.280
Deploy the left-flanked 2nd and 
3rd Fleets to engage them,

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:12.920
and the 6th Fleet to the alpha 
sector as a detachment.

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:15.820
They've sent a detached force.

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:17.580
Continue our advance.

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:21.530
Focus all attacks on the detached right flank.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:25.460
<i>What do you think such a 
small, detached force can do?</i>

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:29.450
<i>If they're trying to hit us from behind, 
I'll take it out before they can.</i>

00:08:32.520 --> 00:08:35.400
Enemy fleet is focusing 
attacks on our left flank.

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:37.360
Return fire while falling back.

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:40.330
The enemy is continuing evasive movement!

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:43.530
Close the distance! Continue to attack!

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:52.870
It's over now!

00:08:58.050 --> 00:08:59.490
Status report!

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:02.420
The enemy's detached force has 
attacked our supply unit.

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:05.810
As far as the simulation goes, 
that means we have ceased to function.

00:09:08.930 --> 00:09:10.100
You're kidding me...

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:11.490
Wideborn lost?

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:16.280
<u>Free Planets Fleet Academy Headmaster
</u>Vice Admiral Sidney Sithole

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:18.440
<i>Winner: Yang Wen-li.</i>

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:22.450
<u></u>Deputy Adjutant General's Office

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:26.480
I would rather not transfer to the 
Strategic Studies Department.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:29.920
<u>Free Planets Fleet Academy Deputy Adjutant General
</u>Lieutenant Alex Cazerne

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:32.690
Didn't your instructor tell you?

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:35.950
The moment you entered this 
school, you became a soldier.

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:38.130
You are to obey orders.

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:40.350
Yes, he told me.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:43.090
Then there's only one thing I can tell you.

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:46.210
If you don't want to do it, 
you have the right to quit.

00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:50.790
But you'd need to repay all the student 
loans you've received thus far.

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:56.080
Don't be so disappointed.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:10:00.490
You defeated Wideborn, the head of your 
class, in the strategic warfare simulation.

00:10:01.090 --> 00:10:03.470
This just means you've been 
recognized for your achievements.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:06.940
There are many talented students in 
the Strategic Studies Department.

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:08.970
Many want to get in, but can't.

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:13.670
I am honored, but I'm no talented student.

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:15.880
Don't be cynical.

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:20.530
Yang Wen-li.

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:25.610
Come by to play chess with me sometimes.

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:28.760
Yes, sir.

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:30.470
I'd be honored.

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:39.420
Hey, you sure you don't wanna come?

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:42.620
My mom's cooking is pretty damn good.

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:45.200
I appreciate it, but don't worry about me.

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:46.270
I see.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:51.190
I actually invited Jessica, 
too, but she shot me down.

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:53.370
She's probably busy with schoolwork.

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:54.780
Yeah.

00:10:55.190 --> 00:10:57.950
I'll have to enjoy this 
break for the both of you.

00:11:15.530 --> 00:11:18.160
You're here to practice your violin again?

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:22.010
And you're here to read history books?

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:22.890
Yeah.

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:25.750
You're a total history nut.

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:30.800
Hey, what is it you're looking at?

00:11:32.470 --> 00:11:34.320
Your eyes are always fixed on the past.

00:11:34.890 --> 00:11:36.870
Isn't there anything else you want to do?

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:48.330
I want to keep my eyes on the future.

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:26.870
I worked up the nerve to confess 
to Jessica before we leave here.

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:29.300
Did you? That's good to hear.

00:12:30.070 --> 00:12:31.810
No, she shot me down.

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:33.270
Why?

00:12:34.130 --> 00:12:36.880
She said she didn't want to 
be a soldier's girlfriend.

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:39.510
I see...

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:42.570
She graduates next year.

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:45.760
She's always said she wanted 
to be a music teacher.

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:47.700
I see...

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:55.320
I want to keep my eyes on the future.

00:12:57.940 --> 00:13:00.480
I guess it's goodbye to this town, huh?

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:01.340
Yeah.

00:13:02.410 --> 00:13:04.070
It was a nice town.

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:27.610
<u></u>One Year Later

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:32.540
<u></u>Free Planets Alliance Navy Space Pier

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:38.950
<i>Sheesh...</i>

00:13:39.450 --> 00:13:42.800
<i>Who knew I'd be assigned to 
front-line duty so soon?</i>

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:56.140
<u></u>The Planet El Facil

00:13:57.750 --> 00:13:58.970
<i>This is a special bulletin.</i>

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:02.810
<i>According to personnel affiliated 
with Garrison Command Headquarters,</i>

00:14:02.810 --> 00:14:04.940
<i>the Imperial Navy appeared to fall back</i>

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:09.660
<i>after contact with our forces, 
only to attack us from behind.</i>

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:15.120
<i>Commander Lynch has ordered an 
immediate retreat here to El Facil.</i>

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:17.590
What? How can that be?

00:14:17.590 --> 00:14:18.580
Retreat?

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:22.550
Weren't they out there 
fighting to protect us all?

00:14:22.970 --> 00:14:27.150
<i>The Galactic Imperial Navy has 
already proclaimed that they</i>

00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:31.840
<i>"will free El Facil from the 
rebel forces within 24 hours."</i>

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:35.980
<u></u>El Facil Garrison Base - Command Room

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:35.630
The enemy fleet has exceeded 
2,000 in number!

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:40.300
Damn that Lynch! He turned tail and 
led the enemy right back to us!

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:44.180
Does he want all three million people 
on El Facil to be killed, too?!

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:48.150
Commander, civilians are 
rushing our space port!

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:51.970
What's going on?!

00:14:51.970 --> 00:14:54.320
The Imperial Army is right on top of us!

00:14:54.320 --> 00:14:57.530
If the garrison is back, let us on it!

00:14:57.530 --> 00:14:59.220
Send out the shuttles already!

00:14:59.220 --> 00:15:00.760
Get whoever's responsible out here!

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:03.160
Yeah! Get them out here!

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:08.710
Who the hell are you?!

00:15:08.710 --> 00:15:10.560
Bring us whoever's responsible for this!

00:15:11.020 --> 00:15:15.950
I'm the one who's been assigned 
responsibility for the escape plan.

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:17.790
Huh? You?

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:27.890
<i>Shuttle maintenance and inspections 
are essentially complete.</i>

00:15:27.890 --> 00:15:28.910
Roger.

00:15:32.900 --> 00:15:33.910
Here.

00:15:35.890 --> 00:15:37.090
Thanks.

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:47.010
You're a big help.

00:15:47.010 --> 00:15:51.000
I don't like coffee, though, 
so I wish you had brought tea.

00:15:55.840 --> 00:15:56.630
Yes.

00:15:57.690 --> 00:15:59.140
<i>Sub-lieutenant Yang...</i>

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:00.730
<i>I don't want to believe it,</i>

00:16:00.730 --> 00:16:04.440
<i>but the garrison fleet just 
left port without us.</i>

00:16:04.870 --> 00:16:07.190
All right, understood.

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:09.900
Then please send everyone 
at command over here, too.

00:16:10.220 --> 00:16:11.440
<i>"Over here"?</i>

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:14.940
<i>Sub-lieutenant, are you aware 
of our situation? Hey—</i>

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:17.840
Come on. We're leaving port.

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:26.800
The garrison fleet left us behind. 
Can we really make it out of here?

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:28.290
There's no need to worry.

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:33.050
The Imperial Navy is probably capturing 
the garrison fleet as we speak.

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:38.710
While they fight, we'll have plenty 
of time to make an easy escape.

00:16:50.700 --> 00:16:54.650
Are you saying... you used 
Commander Lynch as a decoy?

00:16:59.070 --> 00:17:01.000
Now, let's go.

00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:14.010
<u></u>Free Planets Alliance Navy Integrated Tactical Operations Center

00:17:15.290 --> 00:17:17.590
<i>Hey, hero of El Facil.</i>

00:17:17.590 --> 00:17:18.960
Cut it out, Jean.

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:21.080
<i>Congrats on the promotion.</i>

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:22.880
You heard already?

00:17:23.410 --> 00:17:26.080
I was just promoted to 
lieutenant this morning,

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:29.970
but another notice came out at 1 PM that 
I'm being promoted to rear admiral.

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:34.560
<i>Moving up two ranks usually isn't 
allowed unless you've died in battle.</i>

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:35.810
<i>Must be a special exception.</i>

00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:42.460
<i>Well, it sounds like even heroes don't get 
a break from writing reports and vouchers,</i>

00:17:42.460 --> 00:17:44.250
<i>but do you wanna ditch 
for a bit and meet up?</i>

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:46.860
What? Where are you?

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:55.500
I'm no hero.

00:17:56.210 --> 00:17:59.060
I offered Rear Admiral Lynch my opinions,

00:17:59.060 --> 00:18:01.150
but he wouldn't even listen.

00:18:01.150 --> 00:18:04.010
He sent me off the ship 
before the battle started.

00:18:04.940 --> 00:18:08.850
That's why I was able to 
get the people to safety.

00:18:09.470 --> 00:18:15.690
Still, who would think to use Rear Admiral 
Lynch's flight to save everyone?

00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:18.560
That's not something just 
anyone could come up with.

00:18:19.230 --> 00:18:21.190
If I may put on airs for a moment,

00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:26.530
there's nothing more dangerous than being 
too set on one's own rigid opinions.

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:31.910
This reminded me of the 
time you beat Wideborn.

00:18:35.320 --> 00:18:38.950
I learned from history, that's all.

00:18:39.810 --> 00:18:44.350
The basic nature of war hasn't changed in 
the past three or four thousand years.

00:18:44.950 --> 00:18:47.300
Before you reach the battlefield, 
it's your supplies,

00:18:47.300 --> 00:18:50.950
and once you get there, it's the quality 
of your leader that determines victory.

00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:56.250
Yes... Fixing your eyes on past battles

00:18:56.250 --> 00:18:59.040
enables you to predict future battles.

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:04.730
Hanging out with you like this reminds 
me of being at the fleet academy.

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:06.390
It does.

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:11.410
How's Jessica?

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:13.710
I haven't seen her lately.

00:19:14.990 --> 00:19:18.730
I heard she's teaching 
music in Terneuzen now.

00:19:19.210 --> 00:19:20.450
Go see her.

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:35.620
Cadet Yang Wen-li.

00:19:38.350 --> 00:19:40.440
Rear Admiral Alex Cazerne!

00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:43.780
Thank you for arranging all this for me.

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:48.110
I've been looking after you since your 
Fleet Academy days. I'm used to it.

00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:50.760
Here. To celebrate your promotion.

00:19:50.760 --> 00:19:52.950
Welcome to Silverbridge Street.

00:19:52.950 --> 00:19:54.330
Thank you.

00:19:55.430 --> 00:19:57.890
Since we're neighbors now and all,

00:19:57.890 --> 00:20:01.550
I hope you'll work on your 
chess skills a bit.

00:20:09.930 --> 00:20:12.180
Damn, talk about fancy digs.

00:20:12.180 --> 00:20:16.740
I've got two daughters, but my house 
isn't much bigger than this.

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:18.660
It's too big for me.

00:20:19.430 --> 00:20:24.110
I guess you'll have to either 
get married or adopt a kid.

00:20:24.560 --> 00:20:25.750
Adopt?

00:20:27.170 --> 00:20:29.950
You're as clueless as ever.

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:31.290
Just think about it.

00:20:31.710 --> 00:20:37.290
The Free Planets Alliance has been at war 
with the Galactic Empire for 150 years.

00:20:37.720 --> 00:20:43.300
That's naturally going to bring about 
a lot of casualties and war orphans.

00:20:44.060 --> 00:20:48.670
That's why we have the Special Provision for 
the Welfare of Children of Soldiers Law,

00:20:49.500 --> 00:20:53.210
also known as Travers's Law after 
the one who came up with it.

00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:57.120
Orphaned children can be raised 
by other military families,

00:20:57.120 --> 00:21:00.210
and the government offers a loan 
to aid in the expenses.

00:21:00.590 --> 00:21:02.430
If, when the child turns fifteen,

00:21:02.890 --> 00:21:08.130
they apply to become a child soldier 
or attend a military school,

00:21:08.130 --> 00:21:10.710
the loan is entirely forgiven.

00:21:11.380 --> 00:21:13.940
It kills two birds with one stone

00:21:13.940 --> 00:21:17.910
by saving orphaned children and 
securing future military personnel.

00:21:17.910 --> 00:21:19.640
I see.

00:21:19.640 --> 00:21:24.870
But I could hardly call a bachelor 
such as myself a "military family."

00:21:25.350 --> 00:21:27.530
It still works if you're single.

00:21:27.530 --> 00:21:31.850
You can just think of it as a 
medieval-style apprenticeship.

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:35.050
You're telling me I should 
take an apprentice?

00:21:36.200 --> 00:21:41.490
Even a guy like you would have a lot to 
teach a kid, if you lived long enough.

00:21:42.710 --> 00:21:48.580
Actually, you might have even more 
to learn from your apprentice.

00:21:53.260 --> 00:21:55.260
<i>Looks like your life's finally calmed down.</i>

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:58.330
This town has a good library, too.

00:21:58.330 --> 00:21:59.660
I like it.

00:22:00.180 --> 00:22:01.630
<i>You never change.</i>

00:22:02.090 --> 00:22:04.600
<i>I just found out I'm being 
sent on an urgent campaign,</i>

00:22:05.380 --> 00:22:06.430
<i>and...</i>

00:22:06.430 --> 00:22:07.380
What is it?

00:22:09.520 --> 00:22:12.470
<i>Jessica and I talked about this a lot.</i>

00:22:13.580 --> 00:22:15.840
<i>When I come back, we'll be formally engaged.</i>

00:22:29.140 --> 00:22:31.600
What is it you're looking at?

00:22:48.650 --> 00:22:49.980
It's freezing...

00:22:57.110 --> 00:22:58.410
Yes?

00:22:58.410 --> 00:23:00.680
Who is that so early in the morning?

00:23:08.760 --> 00:23:10.880
Coming! One second!

00:24:50.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>Episode 5</b>

00:24:50.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>Birth of the 13th Fleet</b>

00:24:50.770 --> 00:24:55.240
Next time on Legend of 
 the Galactic Heroes - Die Neue These<i>,</i>

00:24:55.240 --> 00:24:59.370
episode five, "Birth of the 13th Fleet."
